# 6. BOOKING CONCURRENCY AND DATA INTEGRITY

Prevent double bookings.

A simple frontend check is not sufficient.

Implement server-side availability validation and transactional booking creation.

When two customers attempt to reserve the same barber and time simultaneously:
- Only one conflicting appointment may be confirmed.
- The other customer must receive a clear message and choose another available slot.

Use appropriate PostgreSQL constraints, transactions, locking, exclusion constraints, or another reliable concurrency-control strategy.

Handle overlapping appointments correctly, including appointments with different durations.

Use a safe booking lifecycle:
- Pending, if a genuine temporary hold mechanism is implemented.
- Confirmed.
- Cancelled.
- Completed.
- No-show.

Do not leave appointments pending indefinitely.

If temporary holds are implemented, enforce their expiration in the backend. Never rely solely on browser timers.

Define which statuses consume availability. Cancelled appointments must release their slots.

A customer must not be able to alter another customer's appointment by changing a booking ID in the browser.

Recalculate service duration, pricing, staff availability, and business rules on the server rather than trusting client-submitted values.

